    "created_at": "2026-09-24T14:01:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-24T15:26:58Z",
    "body": "> @zcorpan: Can you merge this?\r\n\r\nScratch that. I tried implementing this in Gecko and it doesn't fix the issue. I don't even think that this is what Blink does. It looks like Blink _always_ scrolls to the fragment in this, case. So it's not about restoring a scroll position.\r\n\r\n[continuing]\r\nIt's rather about detecting that state _wasn't_ persisted, and in that case scroll to fragment in the indicated part isn't null. Currently there isn't such a check for if something was persisted at all, which is what is required to match Blink's behavior.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
